[36m(TaskRunner pid=147947)[0m ### **Step 1: Prime Factorization of $ 9! $**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=147947)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=147947)[0m We begin by computing the value of $ 9! $ and its prime factorization:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=147947)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=147947)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=147947)[0m 9! = 362880
[36m(TaskRunner pid=147947)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=147947)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=147947)[0m To understand the possible divisors, we factor it into primes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=147947)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=147947)[0m - Number of 2s: $ \lfloor 9/2 \rfloor + \lfloor 9/4 \rfloor + \lfloor 9/8 \rfloor = 4 + 2 + 1 = 7 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=147947)[0m - Number of 3s: $ \lfloor 9/3 \rfloor + \lfloor 9/9 \rfloor = 3 + 1 = 4 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=147947)[0m - Number of 5s: $ \lfloor 9/5 \rfloor = 1 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=147947)[0m - Number of 7s: $ \lfloor 9/7 \rfloor = 1 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=147947)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=147947)[0m Thus,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=147947)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=147947)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=147947)[0m 9! = 2^7 \times 3^4 \times 5 \times 7
